  "# ADR-2608180100: two live outages whose only cause was a configuration value nobody updated

## Status

accepted (2026-08-18)

## Context

The owner asked what of shinshi.club's operation is actually automated. Measuring
that turned up two production outages, neither of which anything had reported.

**Both were dark, not broken.** No test failed, no gate went red, no bot noticed.
The club-shinshi workforce has ten resident bots on 6-24h cadences, and on the day
these were found four of its last turns had failed outright and the other six had
returned `Provider returned no final answer ... No write or external effect was
attempted`. QA's own last turn was an `internal-error`. Nothing in that loop was
positioned to see either outage, and nothing in it could have fixed one: 72 of the
fleet's 74 bots carry `writes=false`.

### Outage 1 — the site's headline feature answered 502 to every visitor

`POST /xrpc/ai.gftd.apps.shinshi.agentChat` returned
`502 {\"error\":\"chat gateway error\",\"upstreamStatus\":500}`.

`companion.cljs` sent `model: \"qwen3.6-35b-a3b\"`, a concrete id hardcoded
2026-07-15. Measured against the live gateway with a chat-scope token:

    model=qwen3.6-35b-a3b -> 500  SyntaxError: Unexpected token 'e',
                                  \"error code: 502\" is not valid JSON
    model=murakumo-main   -> 200  real Japanese text, Qwen3.8-27B-Q4_K_M.gguf

The concrete model's tunnel 502s; the bridge cannot parse that non-JSON body and
returns 500. **The murakumo KV registry still lists `qwen3.6-35b-a3b` as
`status: \"serving\"`**, so the registry could not be used to notice this either --
a self-declaration is not a measurement.

ADR-2607173100 already forbids exactly this (`concrete な model id を … ハード
コードしない`, resolve `murakumo-main` instead). The rule existed and was violated,
and **the test suite pinned the violation**: `companion_test.cljs` asserted
`(= \"qwen3.6-35b-a3b\" (:model body))` with the comment `公式常駐モデル`. A test
that asserts the bug keeps the bug.

### Outage 2 — image generation had been 503 for 20 days

`POST api.murakumo.cloud/v1/images/generations` returned
`503 {\"error\":\"no GATEWAY_URL configured\"}`, surfacing on shinshi.club's
`requestScene` as `502 upstreamStatus:503`.

`local-murakumo`'s `wrangler.toml` left `GATEWAY_URL` unset on 2026-07-29 when
`gateway.gftd.ai` was retired -- a correct decision at the time, taken so the path
would fail honestly rather than point at a host that 502s. The comment recorded
what was needed to restore it: *a Cloudflare DNS/Tunnel decision about which
hostname fronts them, not a value here.*

**That decision was made on 2026-08-07.** `gateway.murakumo.cloud` (Tunnel
c75a3e83 -> comfy-openai-bridge on gad:8189 -> ComfyUI on gad:8188) was created
and documented in `cloud-murakumo/services/comfy-openai-bridge/README.md`, which
records that it restored image generation for awai.network the same day. Nothing
carried it back into this config, so for 11 more days the note asked for a
decision that already existed.

Measured link by link before changing anything:

    api.murakumo.cloud/v1/images/generations -> 503 no GATEWAY_URL configured
    gateway.murakumo.cloud/health            -> 200 {\"ok\": true}
    gad:8189 (bridge) /health                -> 200 {\"ok\": true}
    gad:8188 (ComfyUI) /system_stats         -> 200
    POST gateway.murakumo.cloud/v1/images/generations
                                             -> 200, 789,992-byte PNG in 51s

**Only the first link was broken.** The GPUs, the tunnel, the bridge and the models
were all healthy the entire time, and the whole outage was one absent string.

## Decision

1. **`companion.cljs` resolves the alias.** `default-chat-model` is
   `\"murakumo-main\"`; `MURAKUMO_CHAT_MODEL` overrides it at the call site so a
   single deployment can still be pinned for an experiment without a code edit.
   The test now asserts the alias plus a shape check -- no parameter-count in the
   id -- so it fails on ANY concrete id rather than only on this one.
   Landed `d008d72` (network-awai/club-shinshi-app).
2. **`GATEWAY_URL = \"https://gateway.murakumo.cloud\"`** in local-murakumo's
   `[vars]`, with the stale note replaced by the measured chain and the date the
   tunnel decision was actually made. Landed `071d587`.
3. **`/v1/workflows/run` is NOT restored and is not claimed to be.** The bridge's
   `do_POST` serves `/v1/images/generations` only, so that path moves from an
   honest 503 to the bridge's 404. Both are honest; neither works. A caller needing
   custom ComfyUI graphs should extend `build_workflow`, not add a second gateway.

## Consequences

Verified after deploy, against the public surface, not against a build:

    shinshi.club agentChat        -> 200, real persona reply (41s)
    api.murakumo.cloud images     -> 200, 923,079-byte PNG (35s)
    shinshi.club requestScene     -> 200 {\"url\":\"/b/6792f807...\"}
    GET that url                  -> 200, 1,708,790 bytes, image/png
    scene-drain --chars 1         -> 5/5 generated, 0 failures
    coverage before -> after      -> zero 873->872, complete 489->490,
                                     drainRemaining 977->976

The drain moving is the part that matters: the site's own coverage endpoint
confirms the loop closes, so the remaining 976 undrained characters are now a
question of running the batch, not of a broken capability.

**Chat latency is 41s and that is not fixed here.** `murakumo-main` is one
production slot on Qwen3.8-27B. A 41-second first token is a product problem even
though the endpoint is now correct; recording it rather than letting `200 OK` read
as `healthy`.

## What actually generalizes

Both outages have the same shape, and it is not `someone wrote the wrong value`:

> **The value was right when it was written. The world moved and the value did
> not, and nothing was watching the join.**

A concrete model id is correct until the fleet swaps. `GATEWAY_URL` unset is
correct until a tunnel exists. Neither config was ever edited into a wrong state;
both simply stopped being true, silently, while continuing to look deliberate --
each carried a confident comment explaining why it was that way.

Three things follow, none of which is `be more careful`:

1. **An alias is not a style preference, it is where the staleness is allowed to
   live.** ADR-2607173100 exists so that exactly one place has to be updated when
   the fleet changes. Every consumer that inlines a concrete id re-opens the hole
   the alias was dug to close.
2. **A test that asserts today's value pins today's value.** The chat test was
   green throughout the outage because it asserted the broken constant. Assert the
   *property* (`resolves an alias`, `carries no parameter-count`) rather than the
   current literal.
3. **A comment describing a pending decision needs an expiry, because it will
   outlive the decision.** The `GATEWAY_URL` note was accurate for nine days and
   misleading for eleven, and it read identically in both periods. The reader
   cannot tell those apart, which is the same failure mode ADR-2608136000 names
   for gates: `測れなかった` and `測って問題が無かった` returning the same value.

**No new gate is landed here.** ADR-2608136000 is explicit that a gate is not
landed until it has been seen to fail for the right reason and to pass on the real
distributed tree, and neither of these checks has been built or discriminated yet.
The honest statement is that these two outages were found by measuring, not by a
detector, and that a detector for `a live endpoint that a config claims is
configured` does not exist yet. Writing one is follow-up work, not a claim of this
ADR.

## Follow-ups (named, not done)

- A probe that asks each declared gateway URL whether it answers, and reports
  `unanswered` distinctly from `answered badly` -- the evidence-floor idiom from
  ADR-2608136000. Must be discriminated in both directions before landing.
- Chat latency: one slot on Qwen3.8-27B gives ~41s. Either more slots, a smaller
  model for companion chat, or a streamed response.
- The 976 remaining undrained characters: `tools/scene-drain.cljs` is resumable and
  now works, but nothing schedules it.
- `/signup` returns 404 on shinshi.club -- it is in `routes/segments` but not in
  `root-pages`. A conversion funnel answering 404 is its own finding, unrelated to
  these two, and is not fixed here.
- The club-shinshi bot workforce runs on `murakumo-main` and cannot complete a
  tool-calling turn (21 `provider/invalid-tool-arguments`, 21 `internal-error`
  across the fleet's 74 bots). Until that is addressed the workforce is not a
  detector for anything."}]
